msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:14
msgid "Installing on Windows (source) - how-to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:17
msgid ""
"Building ROS from source on Windows lets you use a development checkout with "
"the tools and dependencies needed for compilation. In this article, you will "
"learn how to prepare Windows, install prerequisites, fetch the source code, "
"build the workspace, and run examples. After you follow these steps, you "
"will have a working ROS source installation on Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:27
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:29
msgid ""
"This page explains how to setup a development environment for ROS 2 on "
"Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:32
msgid "System requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:35
msgid "Language support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:37
msgid ""
"Make sure you have a locale which supports ``UTF-8``. For example, for a "
"Chinese-language Windows installation, you may need to install an `English "
"language pack <https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/language-packs-"
"for-windows-a5094319-a92d-18de-5b53-1cfc697cfca8>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:41
msgid "Create a location for the ROS 2 installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:43
msgid ""
"This location will contain both the installed binary packages, plus the ROS "
"2 installation itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:45
msgid ""
"Start an Administrator Command Prompt session (usually by clicking on the "
"start menu, then typing ``command prompt``, then right-click and ``Run as "
"administrator``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:47
msgid ""
"Then create a directory to store the installation. Because of Windows path-"
"length limitations, this should be as short as possible. We'll use ``C:"
"\\dev`` for the rest of these instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:51
msgid "$ mkdir C:\\dev"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:56
msgid "Increase the Windows maximum path length"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:58
msgid ""
"By default, Windows is restricted to a maximum path length (MAX_PATH) of 260 "
"characters. The ROS 2 build will use significantly longer path lengths, so "
"we will increase that. Using the session you started above, run the "
"following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:62
msgid ""
"$ powershell New-ItemProperty -Path \"HKLM:"
"\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\FileSystem\" -Name "
"\"LongPathsEnabled\" -Value 1 -PropertyType DWORD -Force"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:67
msgid "Execute as administrator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:69
msgid ""
"You can read more about this limitation in `Microsoft's documentation "
"<https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/fileio/maximum-file-path-"
"limitation?tabs=registry>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:71
msgid ""
"Close the administrator terminal and follow using a new Command Prompt "
"session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:74
msgid "Install prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:77
msgid "Install MSVC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:79
msgid ""
"In order to compile the ROS 2 code, the MSVC compiler must be installed. "
"Currently it is recommended to use MSVC 2022."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:82
msgid ""
"Continue using the previous session, and run the following command to "
"download it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:84
msgid ""
"$ powershell irm https://aka.ms/vs/17/release/vs_buildtools.exe -OutFile "
"vs_buildtools_2022.exe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:88
msgid "Now install MSVC 2022:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:90
msgid ""
"$ .\\vs_buildtools_2022.exe --quiet --wait --norestart --add Microsoft."
"Component.MSBuild --add Microsoft.Net.Component.4.6.1.TargetingPack --add "
"Microsoft.Net.Component.4.8.SDK --add Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component."
"CoreBuildTools --add Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.Roslyn.Compiler --add "
"Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.TextTemplating --add Microsoft.VisualStudio."
"Component.VC.CLI.Support --add Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC."
"CoreBuildTools --add Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.CoreIde --add "
"Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component.VC.Redist.14.Latest --add Microsoft."
"VisualStudio.Component.VC.Tools.x86.x64 --add Microsoft.VisualStudio."
"Component.Windows11SDK --add Microsoft.VisualStudio.Component."
"Windows11SDK.22621 --add Microsoft.VisualStudio.ComponentGroup.NativeDesktop."
"Core --add Microsoft.VisualStudio.Workload.MSBuildTools --add Microsoft."
"VisualStudio.Workload.VCTools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:95
msgid ""
"Now wait for a few minutes as the installation of MSVC can take a long time, "
"and there is no feedback while it is progressing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:97
msgid ""
"Once you are able to verify the installation path existence with the "
"following check:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:99
msgid ""
"$ \"%ProgramFiles(x86)%\\Microsoft Visual Studio\\Installer\\vswhere.exe\" -"
"products * -version \"[17.0,18.0)\" -requires Microsoft.VisualStudio."
"Component.VC.Tools.x86.x64 -property installationPath"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:103
msgid ""
"If you see a installation path (``C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Visual "
"Studio\\2022\\BuildTools``), you can continue to the next installation "
"steps. If not, you'll just need to wait a bit longer and try checking the "
"path again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:107
msgid "Install pixi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:109
msgid ""
"ROS 2 uses `conda-forge <https://conda-forge.org/>`__ as a backend for "
"packages, with `pixi <https://pixi.sh/latest/>`__ as the frontend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:113
msgid ""
"The installation of conda-forge may trigger Windows Defender to treat it as "
"a threat, but this can be safely ignored by clicking \"More info\" and \"Run "
"anyway\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:115
msgid ""
"Use use the instructions on https://pixi.sh/latest/ to install ``pixi`` "
"either with the Windows Installer or using command line in your opened "
"Command Prompt terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:117
msgid ""
"Once ``pixi`` has been installed, close the Command Prompt session and start "
"it again, which will ensure ``pixi`` is on the PATH."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:120
msgid "Install dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:122
msgid ""
"Download the pixi configuration file in the existing Command Prompt session:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:124
msgid ""
"$ cd C:\\dev\n"
"$ powershell irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ros2/ros2/refs/heads/"
"rolling/pixi.toml -OutFile pixi.toml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:129
msgid "Install dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:131
msgid "$ pixi install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:136
msgid "Build ROS 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:138
msgid "You can use the same Windows Command Prompt for the build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:141
msgid "Source the MSVC compiler"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:143
msgid ""
"This is required in the Command Prompt you'll use to compile ROS 2, but it "
"is *not* required when running:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:145
msgid ""
"$ call \"C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Microsoft Visual "
"Studio\\2022\\BuildTools\\VC\\Auxiliary\\Build\\vcvarsall.bat\" x86_amd64"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:150
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:209
msgid "Source the pixi environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:152
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:211
msgid ""
"This is required in every Command Prompt you open to set up paths to the "
"dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:154
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:213
msgid ""
"$ cd C:\\dev\n"
"$ pixi shell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:160
msgid "Get ROS 2 code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:162
msgid ""
"Now that we have the development tools we can get the ROS 2 source code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:164
msgid "Setup a development folder, for example ``C:\\dev\\rolling``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:166
msgid ""
"$ md C:\\dev\\rolling\\src\n"
"$ cd C:\\dev\\rolling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:171
msgid ""
"Get the ``ros2.repos`` file which defines the repositories to clone from:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:173
msgid ""
"$ vcs import --input https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ros2/ros2/rolling/"
"ros2.repos src"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:178
msgid "Install additional RMW implementations (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:180
msgid ""
"The default middleware that ROS 2 uses is ``Fast DDS``, but the middleware "
"(RMW) can be replaced at build or runtime. See the :doc:`guide <../RMW-"
"Implementations/Working-with-multiple-RMW-implementations>` on how to work "
"with multiple RMWs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:184
msgid "Build the code in the workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:188
msgid "To build the ``\\rolling`` folder tree:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:190
msgid "$ colcon build --merge-install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:196
msgid ""
"We're using ``--merge-install`` here to avoid a ``PATH`` variable that is "
"too long at the end of the build. If you're adapting these instructions to "
"build a smaller workspace then you might be able to use the default behavior "
"which is isolated install, i.e. where each package is installed to a "
"different folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:201
msgid ""
"Source installation can take a long time given the large number of packages "
"being pulled into the workspace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:204
msgid "Setup environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:206
msgid "Start a new Windows Command Prompt, which will be used in the examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:219
msgid "Source the ROS 2 environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:221
msgid ""
"This is required in every Command Prompt you open to setup the ROS 2 "
"workspace:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:223
msgid "$ call C:\\dev\\rolling\\install\\local_setup.bat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:227
msgid ""
"This will automatically set up the environment for any DDS vendors that "
"support was built for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:229
msgid ""
"It is normal that the previous command, if nothing else went wrong, outputs "
"``The system cannot find the path specified.`` exactly once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:232
msgid "Try some examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:234
msgid ""
"Note that the first time you run any executable you will have to allow "
"access to the network through a Windows Firewall popup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:236
msgid "You can run the tests using this command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:238
msgid ""
"$ cd C:\\dev\\rolling\n"
"$ colcon test --merge-install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:245
msgid ""
"``--merge-install`` should only be used if it was also used in the build "
"step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:247
msgid "Afterwards you can get a summary of the tests using this command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:249
msgid "$ colcon test-result"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:253
msgid ""
"To run the examples, first open a clean new Command Prompt and set up the "
"workspace by sourcing the ``local_setup.bat`` file. Then, run a C++ "
"``talker``\\ :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:256
msgid ""
"$ call install\\local_setup.bat\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:261
msgid ""
"In a separate Command Prompt you can do the same, but instead run a Python "
"``listener``\\ :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:263
msgid ""
"$ call install\\local_setup.bat\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_py listener"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:268
msgid ""
"You should see the ``talker`` saying that it's ``Publishing`` messages and "
"the ``listener`` saying ``I heard`` those messages. This verifies both the C+"
"+ and Python APIs are working properly. Hooray!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:274
msgid ""
"It is not recommended to build in the same Command Prompt that you've "
"sourced the ``local_setup.bat``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:277
msgid "Next steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:279
msgid ""
"Continue with the tutorials to configure your environment, create your own "
"workspace and packages, and learn ROS 2 core concepts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:282
msgid "Stay up to date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:284
msgid ""
"See :doc:`Maintaining-a-Source-Checkout` to periodically refresh your source "
"installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:287
msgid "Troubleshoot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:289
msgid ""
"Troubleshooting techniques can be found :ref:`here <windows-"
"troubleshooting>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:292
msgid "Uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:294
msgid ""
"If you installed your workspace with colcon as instructed above, "
"\"uninstalling\" could be just a matter of opening a new terminal and not "
"sourcing the workspace's ``setup`` file. This way, your environment will "
"behave as though there is no Rolling install on your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:297
msgid ""
"If you're also trying to free up space, you can delete the entire workspace "
"directory with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Windows-Development-Setup.rst:299
msgid "$ rmdir /s /q C:\\dev\\rolling"
msgstr ""
